,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.46084218,"data":"# Symbolic Computation (sympy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460843187,"data":"- Algebraic manipulation and simplification\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460844264,"data":"- Solving equations and systems of equations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460845447,"data":"- Symbolic differentiation and integration\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460846496,"data":"- Number theory functions (primes, divisors, modular arithmetic)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460847679,"data":"- Polynomial operations and factorization\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.46084868,"data":"- Working with mathematical expressions symbolically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460849726,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460850658,"data":"# Numerical Computation (numpy):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460851807,"data":"- Array operations and linear algebra\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460852857,"data":"- Efficient numerical calculations for large datasets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460853905,"data":"- Matrix operations and eigenvalue problems\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460854946,"data":"- Statistical computations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460856084,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460857022,"data":"# Mathematical Functions (math):\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460858023,"data":"- Standard mathematical functions (trig, log, exp)\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460859081,"data":"- Constants like pi and e\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460860191,"data":"- Basic operations for single values\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460861276,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460862254,"data":"Best Practices:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460863253,"data":"- Use sympy for exact symbolic answers when possible\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460864547,"data":"- Use numpy for numerical verification and large-scale computation\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460865655,"data":"- Combine symbolic and numerical approaches: derive symbolically, verify numerically\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460866752,"data":"- Document your computational strategy clearly\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.4608678,"data":"- Validate computational results against known cases or theoretical bounds\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460868933,"data":"- For very large exponents (e.g. a^(n!)), use pow(base, exp, mod) or analytical methods — never materialize the full number\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460870773,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460871726,"data":"# Code Robustness Rules:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.46087279,"data":"- Each code cell must be SELF-CONTAINED: re-import and re-define everything you need. If a previous cell errored, its definitions are LOST.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460874019,"data":"- Avoid sympy expressions that grow beyond a few hundred characters. If an expression is exploding, switch to numerical methods (numpy) or modular arithmetic.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460875256,"data":"- For geometry: prefer numpy coordinate models with brute-force verification over pure symbolic or direction-counting approaches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.46087813,"data":"- For number theory / functional equations: compute small cases first (n=1..20) to find patterns before attempting a proof. Brute-force exploration often reveals the structure.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460879421,"data":"- For combinatorics counting: always verify no duplicates — check injectivity explicitly.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460881469,"data":"- If 5+ code cells without progress, STOP and restart with a different approach.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460882616,"data":"- When using Python, prefer converting sympy expressions to int() before passing to Python builtins like pow(), min(), max().\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460883779,"data":"- Common import: from sympy.ntheory.modular import crt (note: sympy.crt does not exist).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460884906,"data":"- If a code cell fails, re-import necessary libraries in the next cell.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460886022,"data":"- sympy.solve() often times out on complex systems. For polynomial systems with \u003e 3 unknowns, prefer numerical methods (scipy fsolve/minimize) or manual algebraic reduction.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460887522,"data":"- Never call sympy.simplify() or sympy.expand() on expressions involving large binomials or products of many terms. Use float() first to check the numerical value.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.46088876,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460889702,"data":"# Library Availability:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":531.460890711,"data":"NOT installed (do NOT import — they WILL fail): pulp, ortools, z3-solver, mip, pyscipopt, pysat, cvxpy, constraint, matplotlib, sklearn.\n"}
